MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear Moreh,

I would recommend against using the word "causal" unless you are referring to something like Mendelian Randomization. I take it that you are referring to whether you can specify a model that includes paths from the SNP to all GWAS phenotypes. That is straightforward to do using the standard lavaan syntax. Keep in mind that you typically can't have a model that estimates paths from the SNPs to all indicators of a factor and additionally estimates paths to the factor. Such a model is typically underidentified.

Also note that the Q statistic for the common factor GWAS compares a model with a path from the SNP to the factor to a model with paths from the SNP to all indicators (but not the factor). This is described in the original Grotzinger at all paper in Nature Human Behaviour, and further discussed in the supplement to the forthcoming de la Fuente paper (see section "Interpreting the Heterogeneity Statistic" and Figure S9). Papers below:

de la Fuente, J., Davies, J., Grotzinger, A. D., Tucker-Drob, E. M., & Deary. (in press). A general dimension of genetic sharing across diverse cognitive traits inferred from molecular data. Nature Human Behaviour. [de la Fuente & Davies contributed equally to this work; Tucker-Drob & Deary jointly directed this work] Link <https://doi.org/10.1101/766600> (to preprint)

Grotzinger, A. D., Rhemtulla, M., de Vlaming, R., Ritchie, S. J., Mallard, T. T.,  Hill, W. D, Ip, H. F., Marioni, R. E., McIntosh, A. M., Deary, I. J., Koellinger, P. D., Harden, K. P., Nivard, M. G., & Tucker-Drob, E. M. (2019). Genomic structural equation modelling provides insights into the multivariate genetic architecture of complex traits. Nature Human Behaviour, 3, 513-525. [Nivard & Tucker-Drob jointly directed this work] Paper <http://rdcu.be/bvn7t> Supplement(Text/Figures) <http://labs.la.utexas.edu/tucker-drob/files/2019/05/Genomic-SEM-Supplement.pdf> Supplement(Tables) <http://labs.la.utexas.edu/tucker-drob/files/2020/01/41562_2019_566_MOESM3_ESM-1.xlsx>

Cheers,

Elliot

