MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

More strict INFO filters are common for LDSC than for GWAS. Poor imputation can bias LDSC estimates for S, which are otherwise expected to be relatively unbiased. Lower quality imputation for GWAS is typically more tolerated because, although power for discovery is reduced relative to directly tagged or well-imputed variants, power is increased relative to removing the SNP entirely.

