Good evening,

Just a quick question in regards to the model fit of common factor models without SNP effects. Do the typical standards of SRMR < .05 and CFI > .95 still apply? I ask as the GitHub example had values outside of these guidelines, as well as my own common factor results which I was able to run without any convergence warnings.

Best,
Moreh

