> In Grotzinger et al we write:
>
> “SRMR values below 0.10 indicate acceptable fit, values less than 0.05 indicate good fit, and a value of 0 indicates perfect fit54 <https://www-nature-com.ezproxy.lib.utexas.edu/articles/s41562-019-0566-x#ref-CR54>.”
>
> “ CFI values of ≥0.90 are typically considered acceptable fit, and values of ≥0.95 are typically considered good model fit51 <https://www-nature-com.ezproxy.lib.utexas.edu/articles/s41562-019-0566-x#ref-CR51>”
>

> These are rules of thumb, not strict cut offs. You can read more about fit indices in texts such as Kline, or by searching for articles in google scholar.
