Hi Sarah,

Were you using the std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE command when running the user specified model? As written I don't believe your model is identified, and the std.lv <http://std.lv> argument isn't available for userGWAS, so I'm wondering if that is causing the error. It also doesn't look like you are including the effect of a SNP in that model which is likely causing additional issues. I might try rewriting the model as below, but you should confirm this actually matches your analytic question:

testmodel <- 'F1 =~ NA*Trait1 + Trait2
             F2 =~ NA*Trait3
             F3 =~ NA*Trait4 + Trait5
             F1~~F3
             F2~~F3
             F1~~F2

             F1~~1*F1
            F2~~1*F2
            F3~~1*F3
           F1~SNP
          F2~SNP
          F3~SNP
             Trait3 ~~ 0*Trait3'

Best,
-Andrew

